  "quality": {
    "score": 83,
    "configured_min_score": 80,
    "issues": [
      "Compare preview-0.png with clip-0-0.png. The broad light and dark facets on the tallest summit change shape through the middle and lower face. Near the smaller pine, the foreground ledge has a different sequence of steps on its way down to the right. These differences affect visible form and coverage at the same nominal frame, even though subject placement and scale look consistent. Checking the two frame-0 capture paths against the same authored geometry is the clearest follow-up.",
      "The four peaks repeat a similar needle profile, with long dark faces and nearly parallel zigzag seams. The hard, broad facets dominate the more varied fine marks and give the range a cut-paper quality. More differentiated shoulders and a few broken, uneven ink deposits following the main folds would make the connected range read more convincingly as brush-painted rock.",
      "The mist establishes a clear depth break, but its thickest strip hides most of the joining feet and softens several bases to a similar degree. The skyline holds the range together while the lower structure reads more like separate wedges. Alternating brief exposed footholds with soft cloud crossings would make the connection clearer."
    ],
